{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexJonesMarkov","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexJonesMarkov","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexCouplingNormalisation","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.GeomSum"],"declarations":18,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexT35.couplingRatio_not_constant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexT35.couplingRatio_not_constant","kind":"theorem","line":210,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/WeakVertexJonesMarkov.lean#L210-L217","doc":"The ratio is **not constant**, so no normalisation constant relates the two couplings —\nthe derivation explains `no_constant_rescaling` rather than repairing it. Witnessed at two\nrational points: `couplingRatio 1 = −96 ≠ couplingRatio 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexT35.couplingRatio_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexT35.couplingRatio_one","kind":"theorem","line":203,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/WeakVertexJonesMarkov.lean#L203-L208","doc":"**The leading value is `−96`, and it is the two Jones exponents.** `G₈(1) = 8` and\n`G₁₂(1) = 12`, so the classical limit of the ratio is `−8·12`. That derives the\nsecond-order leading coefficient of `J − 1` without differentiating anything. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexT35.jones_dev_div_sSq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexT35.jones_dev_div_sSq","kind":"theorem","line":187,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/WeakVertexJonesMarkov.lean#L187-L201","doc":"**`(J − 1)/s² = couplingRatio q`.** No limit and no derivative: the whole comparison\nof the two couplings is one rational function. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexT35.couplingRatio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexT35.couplingRatio","kind":"def","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/WeakVertexJonesMarkov.lean#L183-L185","doc":"The ratio of the two couplings, `−G₈(q)·G₁₂(q)/q¹⁹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexT35.jones_dev_eq_sSq_mul_geom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexT35.jones_dev_eq_sSq_mul_geom","kind":"theorem","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/WeakVertexJonesMarkov.lean#L172-L181","doc":"**The exact relation between the two couplings.** `q²⁰(J − 1) = −(q·s²)·G₈·G₁₂`: the\n`(q − 1)²` that makes `J − 1` second order is exactly the one in `s²`, and what is left\nover is the cyclotomic pair. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexT35.geomCofactor_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexT35.geomCofactor_mul","kind":"theorem","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/WeakVertexJonesMarkov.lean#L169-L170","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexT35.geomCofactor_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexT35.geomCofactor_one","kind":"theorem","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/WeakVertexJonesMarkov.lean#L166-L167","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexT35.geomCofactor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexT35.geomCofactor","kind":"def","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/WeakVertexJonesMarkov.lean#L163-L164","doc":"The cyclotomic cofactor `G_n(q) = 1 + q + ⋯ + q^{n-1}`, so that `G_n(q)(q − 1) = qⁿ − 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexT35.sSq_of_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexT35.sSq_of_sq","kind":"theorem","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/WeakVertexJonesMarkov.lean#L155-L159","doc":"The decay coupling is the *same shape at half scale*: at `q = u²`,\n`s² = (u − u⁻¹)² = h_{1/2}²`. Stated at `u` so it needs no square root and no ordering. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexT35.jonesT35_sub_one_mul_pow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexT35.jonesT35_sub_one_mul_pow","kind":"theorem","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/WeakVertexJonesMarkov.lean#L147-L153","doc":"The same fact with no negative powers: `q²⁰(J − 1) = −(q⁸ − 1)(q¹² − 1)`. This is the\nform the `(q − 1)²` factor is read off. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexT35.jonesT35_sub_one_eq_qDiff_product","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexT35.jonesT35_sub_one_eq_qDiff_product","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/WeakVertexJonesMarkov.lean#L138-L145","doc":"**`J − 1 = −h₄h₆/q¹⁰`.** The canonically-normalised deviation of the weak vertex from\nits classical value is a product of two q-differences, at the two Jones exponents of\n`T(3,5)`, divided by the framing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexT35.weakVertexTrace_eq_jones_markov","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexT35.weakVertexTrace_eq_jones_markov","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/WeakVertexJonesMarkov.lean#L129-L134","doc":"**The Jones–Markov relation for the weak vertex.** `W · [2]_q^{n-1} = q^{2e} · V(q^{-2})`\nat `n = 3`, `e = 10`: the trace *is* the Jones polynomial up to a framing power and the\nMarkov rank factor, both read off the braid word `(σ₀σ₁)⁵`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexT35.jones_framing_eq_numerator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexT35.jones_framing_eq_numerator","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/WeakVertexJonesMarkov.lean#L123-L127","doc":"The framing factor: `q²⁰ · V(q^{-2}) = q¹² + q⁸ − 1` with `e = 10`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexT35.weakVertexTrace_mul_twoQ_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexT35.weakVertexTrace_mul_twoQ_sq","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/WeakVertexJonesMarkov.lean#L117-L121","doc":"The rank factor: `W · [2]_q² = q¹² + q⁸ − 1`, the numerator of the closed form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexT35.qDiff_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexT35.qDiff_one","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/WeakVertexJonesMarkov.lean#L110-L113","doc":"Every q-difference vanishes classically, which is what makes a *product* of two of\nthem vanish to second order. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexT35.qDiff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexT35.qDiff","kind":"def","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/WeakVertexJonesMarkov.lean#L107-L108","doc":"The q-difference `h_k = q^k − q^{-k}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexT35.jonesT35_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexT35.jonesT35_one","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/WeakVertexJonesMarkov.lean#L103-L105","doc":"`V_K(1) = 1` for every knot; here the instance that fixes the offset of `J − 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexT35.jonesT35","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexT35.jonesT35","kind":"def","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/WeakVertexJonesMarkov.lean#L100-L101","doc":"The Jones polynomial of the `(3,5)`-torus knot, `V_{T(3,5)}(t) = t⁴ + t⁶ − t¹⁰`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}